{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/859581-hunting-human-souls","id":859581,"title":"Hunting Human Souls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-05T06:19:16-07:00","id":859581,"title":"Hunting Human Souls","content":"On page 97 at the start of the Primordial Pathways section, it states; &quot;When acting in the Horror\u2019s stead isn\u2019t enough and a Beast wishes to target a human soul as her prey, when her Horror is so hungry it breaks its bonds, or when a Beast exploring kinship wishes to visit the realms wandered by her supernatural cousins, she utilizes a Primordial Pathway.&quot;<br /> <br /> The first part is what interests and confuses me a bit. It seems to imply a method of raising satiety through preying on a victim through a part of the astral, as opposed to in the material world. I could be wrong about this, but the modifiers for opening pathways talk about being able to enter the Temenos, the Anima Mundi, or the Oneiros, so I figure I am on the right track.<br /> <br /> Trouble is, I am not sure how this works , unless I missed something. If it is indeed true they can prey on a victim's soul, how do they go about that mechanically?<br /> <br /> Any help from developers would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T06:27:23-07:00","id":859588,"title":"","content":"It is when you satiety is 3- for a long, then the Horror go out from the lair to hunt dreamer for own sake.<br /> You dont take the &quot;seat&quot;: the Horror go for hunt, alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T06:39:50-07:00","id":859594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/859581-hunting-human-souls?p=859588#post859588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is when you satiety is 3- for a long, then the Horror go out from the lair to hunt dreamer for own sake.<br /> You dont take the &quot;seat&quot;: the Horror go for hunt, alone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except the text seems to imply that what you state, and what I am curious about, are two different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1353-riche","name":"RichE","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:25:11-07:00","id":859732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichE</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/859581-hunting-human-souls?p=859594#post859594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except the text seems to imply that what you state, and what I am curious about, are two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Horror does do that, but you can use a Pathway to 'manually' enter the Temenos and, from there, Oneroi. It's not something all Beasts do (as not all of them are aware that the Temenos exists) but they can do it. I guess they could use that to hunt people in their own dreamscapes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:33:57-07:00","id":859735,"title":"","content":"The exact method will depend on the Beast. A collector could steal something, depriving their victim of a part of their very psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T04:35:54-07:00","id":860226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/859581-hunting-human-souls?p=859735#post859735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exact method will depend on the Beast. A collector could steal something, depriving their victim of a part of their very psyche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. It strikes me that a Tyrant, Nemesis, or Predator doing their thing in dreams could cause a lot less lasting harm to their target (barring the risk of Hero-ing them, which ought to apply to this as well as the Horror feeding itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T04:55:36-07:00","id":860233,"title":"","content":"Maybe not a predator. Eating a bit of someone's mind would have a similar effect to stealing it, most likely. <br /> <br /> Still, it seems like a neat sort of irony. The hunger that causes some of the least direct harm in the material is one of the nastier ones in the astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:30:11-07:00","id":860245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/859581-hunting-human-souls?p=860233#post860233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe not a predator. Eating a bit of someone's mind would have a similar effect to stealing it, most likely. <br /> <br /> Still, it seems like a neat sort of irony. The hunger that causes some of the least direct harm in the material is one of the nastier ones in the astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't have to actually eat a part, only Subject them to the fear of being prey for something monstrous. Easy enough. I mean, out of 10, how many nightmares are about something chasing you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}